======================================================================
#11b  BIREFRINGENCE WINDOW -- residual normal fraction at recombination
======================================================================

  f_n(z_rec) = ((1+z_rec)/(1+z_x))^n ,   z_rec = 1100
  n=4  phonon superfluid (rho_n ~ T^4, the SLOWEST-dying / best case)
  n=2  a soft/optimistic dispersion (still power-law)

         z_x   T_rec/T_c     f_n (n=4)     f_n (n=2)
  ----------------------------------------------------
      100000      0.0110      1.47e-08      1.21e-04
       30000      0.0367      1.81e-06      1.35e-03
       10000      0.1101      1.47e-04      1.21e-02
        3400      0.3237      1.10e-02      1.05e-01
        2000      0.5502      9.17e-02      3.03e-01
        1500      0.7335      2.89e-01      5.38e-01

  window reaches f_n = 1%  (n=4)  at  z_x = 3481   (29x below the model's z_x=1e5)
  window reaches f_n = 1%  (n=2)  at  z_x = 11009   (9x below the model's z_x=1e5)

----------------------------------------------------------------------
VERDICT: at the model's z_x ~ 1e5, f_n(rec) ~ 1e-8 (n=4) -- the open
account is dead ~8 orders before recombination -> birefringence
suppressed ~1e-8 -> WINDOW CLOSED.  It opens (f_n >~ 1%) only if
condensation is pushed down to z_x ~ few x 10^3 (near equality),
~30x lower than the model gives.  So P-009's null holds here too,
UNLESS #11 pins z_x near matter-radiation equality.
----------------------------------------------------------------------
